{
  "english_witnesses": [
    {
      "stem": "tair_vetaria",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:tair_vetaria",
      "title": {
        "he": "תָּעִיר וְתָרִיעַ",
        "en": "תָּעִיר וְתָרִיעַ"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s133",
                "printed_page": "52",
                "text": "Thou dost rise and let the trumpet sound to destroy every evil doer, and Thou art sanctified by those who know how to sound the Teruah, Holy One.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/tair_vetaria/part_1"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "stem": "adderet_mamlakhah",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adderet_mamlakhah",
      "title": {
        "he": "אַדֶּרֶת מַמְלָכָה",
        "en": "אַדֶּרֶת מַמְלָכָה"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s133",
                "printed_page": "52",
                "text": "The glorious realm, how has it been cast down and not yet been restored to rule. It swore allegiance to Bel, it followed him against the law. Thus there gained dominion over it a mighty alien realm, until God’s realm will once again appear. It has burned my sanctuary, it has crushed my upright",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/adderet_mamlakhah/part_1"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "men and has achieved length of rule. It has expanded greatly, stretched the bow and extended far its yoke. It has frightened the tender people (Israel) and trampled it down, and rules to this day. It has loosened and destroyed the foundation stones of the Temple and laid them bare down to the ground. It has lifted up its head, devised a secret plan and stands there powerfully. It is ablaze with guile, raises itself up to heaven and girds itself in majesty. My tapestries has it torn, destroyed my tabernacles, ploughed and harrowed its site. It has acquired dominion, wrapped itself in might and offended this people (Israel). It initiated rebellion, served idols zealously",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/adderet_mamlakhah/part_2"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": "and desecrated the realm of God. It oppressed the King’s children (Israel) and said in the sight of the King: “Who is in heaven my king?”. There is boasting from the royal throne: “There is no king besides me, I alone am king”. O Thou who art exalted above all kings, remove from it the rank of king, so that the kingdom may return to Thee.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/adderet_mamlakhah/part_3"
          }
        ]
      },
      "instructions": [
        {
          "text": "חתום בראשי חרוזים אלעזר בירבי קליר.",
          "type": "description",
          "language": "he",
          "witnesses": [
            "he"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stem": "melekh_memallet",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_memallet",
      "title": {
        "he": "מֶלֶךְ מְמַלֵּט",
        "en": "מֶלֶךְ מְמַלֵּט"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": "O King, Thou savest from misfortune those who understand Teruah, Holy God.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/melekh_memallet/part_1"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "stem": "melekh_zokher_achuz_qeren",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:melekh_zokher_achuz_qeren",
      "title": {
        "he": "מֶלֶךְ זוֹכֵר אֲחוּז קֶרֶן",
        "en": "מֶלֶךְ זוֹכֵר אֲחוּז קֶרֶן"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": "O King, Thou dost remember him (Isaac) who was caught by the horn (the ram) on behalf of those who blow the horn before Thee today, O awe-inspiring and Holy One!",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/melekh_zokher_achuz_qeren/part_1"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "stem": "aafir_nezer",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:aafir_nezer",
      "title": {
        "he": "אַאֽפִּיר נֶֽזֶר",
        "en": "אַאֽפִּיר נֶֽזֶר"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s139",
                "printed_page": "55",
                "text": "I adorn the awe-inspiring with a crown through the threefold sanctification of the day. The strong in might and greatness rejoice before Him in the house of assembly. They who praise in tumultuous throngs, laud Him with glorifying word. To Him who remembers piety for ever, do the Hayoth sing a new song. Praise Him alone — benevolent is He and forgives sins — on the day of the new moon. He suppresses wrath entirely and does not allow anger. O you (the angels) who serve Him in trembling and fear, praise Him who is awe-inspiring in the presence of those (Israel). Angels of fire encircled by the whirlwind, chant in honour of Him who",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/aafir_nezer/part_1"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s141",
                "printed_page": "56",
                "text": "removes wrath. Angels of mystery, open your mouths to praise Him who sees all. Congregations of the holy people, praise Him, tumultuous myriads. Hearken to the loud blast of the Shofar that guilt may be forgiven.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/aafir_nezer/part_2"
          }
        ]
      },
      "instructions": [
        {
          "text": "ע״ס א״ב.",
          "type": "description",
          "language": "he",
          "witnesses": [
            "he"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stem": "teshalesh_shofarot",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:teshalesh_shofarot",
      "title": {
        "he": "תְּשַׁלֵּשׁ שׁוֹפָרוֹת",
        "en": "תְּשַׁלֵּשׁ שׁוֹפָרוֹת"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s141",
                "printed_page": "56",
                "text": "Three times wilt Thou sound the Shofar blast on the holy mountain; three times will I pronounce the sanctification in the Sanctuary.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/teshalesh_shofarot/part_1"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "stem": "shemo_mefoarim",
      "urn": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim",
      "title": {
        "he": "שְׁמוֹ מְפָאֲרִים",
        "en": "שְׁמוֹ מְפָאֲרִים"
      },
      "languages": {
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s133",
                "printed_page": "52",
                "text": "His Name is praised by the community of His portion, His praise is proclaimed by the holy Erelim and in His sanctuary everything utters glory of the Holy One.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/shemo",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 2,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s133",
                "printed_page": "52",
                "text": "Those who observe His commandments will yet return to the fortress, those who fear Him, speak to one another in purity and bliss, and the Lord has listened and heard and it is inscribed in the book of remembrance, the Holy One.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/shomerei",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 3,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s133",
                "printed_page": "52",
                "text": "Improve your deeds that the covenant may not be broken, He who has adorned the skies, will hear your cry, and it will be more pleasing than the sacrifice of oxen to the Lord the Holy One.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/shapru",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 4,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "Let the tribes of those Thou hast called, arise and rule, cut off the branches of enemies and let them fall, for both kingdom and ruler belong to the Lord, the Holy One.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/shivtei",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 5,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "May our exiled ascend from afar His holy mountain that we may praise Him always in His Inner Sanctuary, for He has remembered His holy word, the Holy One.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/shevutenu",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 6,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/kol_yoshvei"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 6,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "All inhabitants of the world and dwellers on earth do constantly say: Great things has the Lord performed on earth, and the Lord shall be King over all the earth, the Holy One.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "conditions": [
              {
                "type": "opensiddur:rite",
                "features": {
                  "metz": false
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 6,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 7,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "Glorification and praise willingly do I bestow, I order prayer in speech and thought, ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/adar"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 7,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "I call upon the supreme God.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/57/3",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/57/3",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/adar_1/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/adar_1/chapter/3"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 7,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": " On the day chosen from the mighty heavens for upright judgment to glorify His holiness, ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 7,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "the Lord rules, the earth rejoices.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/97/1",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/97/1",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/adar_2/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/adar_2/chapter/1"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 7,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": " The world is too small to contain His loftiness, who is there able to describe His might? ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 7,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "King of all the earth is God, then sing with understanding.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/47/8",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/47/8",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/adar_3/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/adar_3/chapter/8",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 8,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "May all His creatures acquire perception and know how great is His might. ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/dea"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 8,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "A memorial has He established for His wonders.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/111/4",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/111/4",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/dea_4/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/dea_4/chapter/4"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 8,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": " He has firmly planted His foundation stone (Torah), the divine gift, so as to rejoice in His people. ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 8,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s135",
                "printed_page": "53",
                "text": "He remembers His covenant for ever.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/111/5",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/111/5",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/dea_5/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/dea_5/chapter/5",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 9,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": "He has inscribed my thoughts through a statute of the faith so as to remember me year by year, for a remembrance in the sanctuary of the Lord.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/varasham",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 10,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": "When the holy sacrifice (Isaac) once found favour in His eyes, He allowed a ram to be sacrificed in his stead, which was later caught with his horns in the thicket. He taught the descendants of (Isaac) to blow the Shofar on this new moon; but if this day falls on a Sabbath, then the mere mention of Teruah is a sacred proclamation. When it falls on a weekday for you, let it be blown in all your regions, let it be a day of Teruah for you.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/zevach",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 11,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": "Exalted is the rock of my salvation in the mouths of all peoples. Expose Thine arm to help us against adversaries, ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/yarum"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 11,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": "Thy realm is a realm of all eternity.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/145/13",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/145/13",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/yarum_6/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/yarum_6/chapter/13"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 11,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": " When Thou revealest Thyself before all eyes to visit once again Thy dwelling place, congregations in their myriads will proclaim aloud: ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 11,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": "The Lord shall reign for ever and ever.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:exodus/15/18",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:exodus/15/18",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/yarum_7/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/yarum_7/chapter/18"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 11,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": " Becoming to Thee is honour and the acknowledgment of might pronounced by the earth and its inhabitants and all the isles: ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 11,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s137",
                "printed_page": "54",
                "text": "who does not fear Thee, King of the nations.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:jeremiah/10/7",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:jeremiah/10/7",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/yarum_8/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/yarum_8/chapter/7",
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 12,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s139",
                "printed_page": "55",
                "text": "Break the yoke of adversaries, destroy them; gather those dispersed by Thee and redeem them without ransom. ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "reference_unit": "stanza",
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/motot"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 12,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s139",
                "printed_page": "55",
                "text": "Remember Thy congregation which Thou hast once chosen.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/74/2",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/74/2",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/motot_9/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/motot_9/chapter/2"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 12,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s139",
                "printed_page": "55",
                "text": " Comfort the noblest of peoples, expose to their faces the shame of those who rise against them; ",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 12,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s139",
                "printed_page": "55",
                "text": "remember, O Lord, against the sons of Edom the day of Jerusalem.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/137/7",
            "source_reference": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/137/7",
            "chapter_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/motot_10/chapter",
            "source_reference_corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:shemo_mefoarim/quotations/motot_10/chapter/7"
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 12,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s139",
                "printed_page": "55",
                "text": " Make even our highway, straighten it for our steps that the foot of Thy favourite may not stumble, as Thou hast said: I will surely still remember him.",
                "page_start": true
              }
            ],
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 13,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s139",
                "printed_page": "55",
                "text": "The joyful city, sanctum and porch, and the altar may He restore with all the sacred vessels; the Lord will reign for ever. Heaven and earth exult at His Name; forests clap their hands in delight in Him; ",
